event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":182,"item_id":"fc_03037c75de7a2c36016adb34340c8c81918d1e0677b0890358","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_input\\\":\\\"prior-candidate.json\\\",\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/2/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"If D=0, choose x₀∈E by H001. Projection F→I is onto and 1-Lipschitz. Mapping covers by this map cannot increase diameters, so dim_H(I)≤dim_H(F). Since I has nonempty interior in ℝ, the pinned interval dimension theorem gives dim_H(I)=1. Thus dim_H(F)≥1=D+1. For n=0, this branch handles the only possible E⊆ℝ⁰: E is the singleton, D=0, and no replacement of zero-diameter covers by positive-diameter subsets of ℝ⁰ is needed. Combine with the upper bound for n≥1.\\\"}]}\"}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":183,"output_index":2,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_03037c75de7a2c36016adb34340c8c81918d1e0677b0890358","call_id":"call_6bc41f7801a749319a3f437130d6c004","name":"check_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_input\\\":\\\"prior-candidate.json\\\",\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/2/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"If D=0, choose x₀∈E by H001. Projection F→I is onto and 1-Lipschitz. Mapping covers by this map cannot increase diameters, so dim_H(I)≤dim_H(F). Since I has nonempty interior in ℝ, the pinned interval dimension theorem gives dim_H(I)=1. Thus dim_H(F)≥1=D+1. For n=0, this branch handles the only possible E⊆ℝ⁰: E is the singleton, D=0, and no replacement of zero-diameter covers by positive-diameter subsets of ℝ⁰ is needed. Combine with the upper bound for n≥1.\\\"}]}\"}","status":"completed"}}

